# Frontend Redesign Implementation Plan

This plan details the procedure for building a brand new, Apple-inspired frontend in the `frontend-new` directory while preserving 100% of the features and API integrations from the current `frontend` folder.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> The new frontend will be built in `frontend-new`. Once the redesign is fully complete and verified, we will replace the old `frontend` folder with `frontend-new`. No changes to GitHub Actions deployment workflows (`deploy.yml`) are needed for now.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Project Initialization & Dependencies
- Initialize a fresh Vite React project inside the `frontend-new` folder (avoiding overwriting the `design system` directory).
- Install necessary dependencies mirroring your current stack (excluding framer-motion): `react-router-dom`, `lucide-react`, `chart.js` (used in the template), and `@uiw/react-md-editor`.
- Install testing libraries: `vitest`, `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/jest-dom`, and `jsdom`.

### 2. Global Design System Configuration
#### [NEW] `frontend-new/src/styles/theme.css`
- Extract the entire `<style>` block from `apple_inspired_dashboard.html`.
- This file will act as the single source of truth for:
  - Light/Dark mode CSS variables (`--bg-base`, `--accent`, etc.)
  - Glassmorphism effects (`backdrop-filter`) and shadows.
  - Global keyframes (`orbFloat`, `spin`, `pulse`). Custom animations will be handled via standard CSS.

#### [NEW] `frontend-new/src/context/ThemeContext.jsx`
- A new context provider to manage light/dark mode toggling by applying `data-theme="dark"` to the `document.documentElement`, precisely as your template requires.

### 3. Core Reusable UI Components
Before building pages, we will build the atomic building blocks from your template:
#### [NEW] `frontend-new/src/components/ui/`
- **`Layout.jsx`**: The main wrapper containing the `Sidebar` and `Topbar` with dynamic routing.
- **`Card.jsx` / `StatCard.jsx`**: The glassmorphic floating cards.
- **`Button.jsx` / `Input.jsx`**: The standardized form elements.
- **`Loader.jsx`**: The elegant ring spinner.
- **`BackgroundOrb.jsx`**: The animated background gradient orb.

### 4. Logic & Utility Migration
#### [MODIFY] `frontend-new/src/utils/` & `context/`
- Directly port `AuthContext.jsx`, `api.js`, and `fetchInterceptor.js` from the old frontend to ensure identical API communication and maintenance mode interception.

### 5. Page Implementations (Feature Parity)
We will rebuild every existing route using the new UI components:

#### [NEW] Authentication & Public Pages
- Rebuild `Login.jsx`, `Signup.jsx`, `ForgotPassword.jsx`, and `LandingPage.jsx`. They will be placed over the animated `BackgroundOrb` with centered glassmorphic cards.

#### [NEW] Dashboards
- **Student Dashboard (`/dashboard`)**: Port the "Ongoing", "Upcoming", and "Completed" exam logic into the new tabbed/grid layout from the template.
- **Admin Dashboard (`/admin/dashboard`)**: Fully implement the admin-specific sidebar navigation (Overview, Users, Results) exactly as visually defined in your `apple_inspired_dashboard.html`.
- **Teacher Dashboard (`/teacher/dashboard`)**: Create a completely separate dashboard view and navigation tailored for teachers (Exams, Assignments, Grading).

#### [NEW] Exam Environment (`/exam/:examId`)
- Rebuild the exam wrapper (which holds the IDE iframe). 
- Copy the `frontend/public/ide` folder entirely into `frontend-new/public/ide` so the Elixir IDE remains fully functional and intact.

### 6. App Wrapper & Maintenance Logic
#### [NEW] `frontend-new/src/App.jsx`
- Setup `react-router-dom` with the new separated route structure.
- Implement the exact same event listeners (`maintenance-lock`, `maintenance-warning`) to handle the freezing UI and countdown timer during server shifts.

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Write test suites for core components using `vitest` and `react-testing-library`.
- Configure the Vite test runner.

### Manual Verification
1. **Local Development**: Run `npm run dev` in `frontend-new` on port `5173`.
2. **Visual QA**: Compare the rendering of the Dashboards in the React app against the raw `apple_inspired_dashboard.html` file.
3. **Functional QA**: Log in as a student, enter an exam, and verify the IDE iframe loads and communicates with the backend correctly.
4. **Maintenance QA**: Trigger the maintenance API and verify the UI freezes with the new Apple-inspired aesthetics.
